        "Reply Two says, “My cousin confirms everything.” Its link opens Reply One. No cousin is named, quoted, or shown.",
        "Reply Three says, “A second angle proves it.” The supposed second angle is the first image flipped from left to right. The EXIT sign is backward.",
        "Reply Four says, “Everyone saw this coming.” It contains a collage of the first three replies. A hundred votes measure reactions to the collage, not the number of original observations.",
        "Far below them, a reply with two votes says, “I was unloading instruments near the west hall at 12:15. The cart was stopped at the cleaning barrier. A staff member scanned its route label and rolled it toward the east entrance.” The writer includes the time, location, and limits of the observation. They do not claim to know why the old route loaded.",
